WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.990
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.510
Panda, Tired of Boredom!

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.240
What's wrong, Panda?

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.440
I don't wanna go to work.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:51.630
It's the rainy season now, 
so there aren't many visitors.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.790
It's so boring and 
there's nothing to do.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:57.730
You're being dramatic.

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:00.320
But all you do is lay around anyway.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.600
It's hard to have nothing to do.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:07.020
Not to mention I'm lying 
around for work.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:10.770
That's different from 
normal lying around.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.110
I have no idea what 
you're talking about.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.200
I want to try having nothing
 to do and lying around, too.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.090
There are times when I'm 
eating a snack slowly

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.930
and only an hour's passed by.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.760
An hour for a snack?

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:29.210
You're like one of those 
rich, old ladies.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:40.200
Hey! What are you doing?

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:44.550
There aren't any visitors, 
so we don't have anything to do.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.600
You even brought in a small table.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.900
Yeah, it was so hard to bring 
it in without being noticed.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.820
You're not supposed to bring it in!

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.930
Oh, relax.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:03.620
How about a cup of healthy
bear bamboo grass tea?

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.080
Bear bamboo grass tea?

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.970
The bamboo grass 
polysaccharides in this tea

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:12.210
are said to have weight 
loss effects, too.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.140
Really?

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:17.130
Well, I have been putting 
on a little weight lately.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:24.070
Hurry and clean all of this up!

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.470
What time is it?

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:34.720
You were asleep?

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.190
Let's see...

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.240
It's only 10 o'clock.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:46.530
What? It's only been 30 minutes?

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:52.290
Bamboo 
Grass

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:52.290
Bamboo Grass

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:52.290
Panda 
Evolution

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.280
In my dream, I'd gotten my idol debut

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.060
and released my first CD.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.180
And at the end of the year, I was even

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:58.220
in the New Year's count down 
live with Yama Arashi.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.800
It must be nice to be able to 
have such pleasing dreams.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.250
So who is Yama Arashi?

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:11.800
You don't know that nationally 
famous idol group?

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.340
They're common knowledge.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.940
That was depressing.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.680
Being told that something is
 common knowledge by Panda

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:21.650
was somehow really depressing.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.130
You have two daughters, right?

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.640
Aren't they fans?

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:30.030
We haven't been talking much, lately.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.240
This is getting really depressing,

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.860
so let's play "hey, look over there."

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:39.840
Sure.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:43.800
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.270
Hey, look over there.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.600
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:52.270
Hey, look over there.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:55.190
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.830
Hey, look over there.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:04:59.650
There.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.320
There...

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:02.980
There...

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.920
Are you mocking me by any chance?

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.700
I think I was sleeping wrong.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:17.330
I can only turn my head to the right.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.590
Hey, what are you making?

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:30.550
A reprint edition model of the
Star Gunner Bismar Ace.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.690
Oh...

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:37.390
Don't say "Oh." 
You sound like my wife.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.660
This is a premium item

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:45.640
and it was really hard to win 
it off the internet auction.

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:49.160
Oh...

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.140
Could you stop it with the "Oh"?

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:55.860
I didn't know you were

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.120
into that kind of stuff, 
Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:01.840
Plastic models are a man's passion.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:07.090
Do you want to see my collection?

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.130
Oh, where is it?

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:19.270
Wow!

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:22.340
I have a lot more at home,

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:26.150
but my family complains that 
they're taking up too much room.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:29.230
Well, you do have two daughters.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.400
Well...

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.480
Oh, what?

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:38.260
My wife has a third in her tummy.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.550
Maybe even a fourth?

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:44.360
Oh, stop!

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.090
Nothing to do.

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:59.600
Hello, this is Polar Bear's Café.

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:01.930
Hey, Polar Bear.

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:05.520
I don't have anything to do, 
so let's play a word connecting game.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.350
I have things to do, though.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:12.240
Okay, I'll start. "Ringo" <i>(apple)</i>.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:15.300
"Goukon" <i>(Group blind date)</i>.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:16.220
A word ending in "n" ends the game.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:27.240
Hello, this is the petting zoo.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.420
Oh, the pandas are missing?

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:35.760
Well, you know,

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.540
pandas need to rest, too.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.520
I'm terribly sorry! 
I'll send them right over!

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:51.920
Get back to work!

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:55.070
How cute!

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.280
Hey, look over here!

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.470
They're our first visitors today,

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:02.210
so I'll give them extra service!

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.850
Service, service.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.630
Service, service.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.630
How cute!

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.410
The pandas are convulsing!

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:15.030
Hurry! We have to get the zoo keeper!

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:20.760
This is depressing.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:23.380
How about we do the usual?

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:25.410
The usual?

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:34.150
Mr. Handa, please hurry and 
come to the Panda Corner.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:36.650
What is this?

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:42.730
What are you doing now?

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:45.410
Do you know how to play 
mahjong, Mr. Handa?

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:46.210
No.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:48.680
Oh, you'll be fine.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.750
I don't know the rules either.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:55.220
It's raining and there aren't 
that many visitors.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:57.620
You don't have anything to do,
 right, Mr. Handa?

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:01.510
Hurry and clean all of this up!

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:04.570
Thank you very much.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:11.220
And then, it was really rough
 because we had nothing to do.

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:14.500
I can't empathize with you at all.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:19.710
I even read the same manga 
thirty times today.

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:22.450
Could I get another café mocha?

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:28.540
Do you know any good ways to 
pass the time, Polar Bear?

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.480
Passing time <i>(himatsubushi)</i>?

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:35.620
Those would be 
eel fillets <i>(hitsumabushi)</i>.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.870
That would be 
dried bonito <i>(katsuobushi)</i>.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:42.260
Oh, the moon...

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:44.100
That would be the 
folk song "Tanko Bushi."

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:48.620
Polar Bear doesn't seem to 
have problems passing the time.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.110
What about you, Miss Sasako?

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:55.900
I like to go on bike rides 
with no set destination.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:10:01.090
I also like to wander around the city
with a map, admiring the sights.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:02.990
What about you guys?

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:06.140
I pop bubble wrap all the time.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:11.980
I read... really long... 
historical novels.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:14.700
Solid black jigsaw puzzles are

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:17.420
hard and can help you forget time.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.720
I envy you all.

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:25.300
I have to rest for twenty hours a day,

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:29.310
so I never have enough 
time when I'm awake.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:32.940
My schedule is really full, too.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:34.290
See?

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:36.280
What?

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.530
Miss Penko is a really hard worker,

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:42.240
and it's really hard to 
visit her everyday.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.550
So I don't have any time at all. And—

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:47.180
Could I get some bamboo 
grass, Polar Bear?

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:49.010
Hey, listen!

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:55.710
And then Miss Penko gave 
me service tickets...

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:58.670
We already heard that 
story too many times.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:03.680
Our store will be closing shortly.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.010
What are you doing?

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:08.140
I wanted to try this at least once.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:11.450
It's already closing time...

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:16.630
Time flies by so fast 
at Polar Bear's Café.

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.990
Oh, I know!

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.070
What?

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:36.340
Mr. Handa, please come to the 
Panda Corner immediately.

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.380
Petting Zoo

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.380
Handa Style         Chocolate Parfait

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.850
What in the world is this?!

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:47.390
Could I get my usual, Mr. Handa?

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.560
Could I get the breakfast 
set, Mr. Handa?

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:53.030
Could I get a chocolate parfait?

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:54.920
I want a mille-feuille.

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:58.070
Could I get a cocoa, Mr. Handa?

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:01.920
Hurry and clean all of this up!

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:05.130
This isn't a café!

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:08.950
Mr... Hand—

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:13.790
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:13.220
Panda's Advice Room for Troubles!

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:26.600
I wonder if it's going to 
rain all day again today.

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:28.380
I was able to write it.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:32.440
A kanji word I was able 
to read but not write.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:36.110
Melancholy

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:36.110
Melan...choly.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.110
Polar 
Bear

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:39.070
Well done, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:43.440
It is rather melancholy 
with all this rain.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.660
Panda

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:02.260
Jeez... I even gave him a cell 
phone so he wouldn't be late.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.180
Mr. Handa!

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:09.180
Hey, Mr. Handa!

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:12.930
Let's play, Mr. Handa!

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:15.960
You're as popular as ever.

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:19.690
I'm popular with animals, 
kids, and old people.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.900
No luck with girls, though.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:29.420
He is the zoo keeper in charge 
of pandas, Mr. Handa.

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:32.580
He works hard everyday 
taking care of the pandas.

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:35.070
His special skill is cooking.

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:37.310
He's a modern guy 
who makes his own lunch.

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:40.880
Number of years having a 
girlfriend: zero.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:42.150
I can hear you.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:44.480
Number of years having a 
girlfriend: zero.

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:47.010
Hey, would you get to work already?

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:50.080
Not to mention you were 
late again today, Panda.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:52.970
I even called you repeatedly 
to wake you up.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:56.440
Mr. Handa, you're such a great guy.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:57.900
Huh?

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:01.570
You even put on a panda strap.

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:05.300
Well, you like pandas, Panda.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:09.410
Or rather, hurry and get to work!

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.510
But I'm worried sick about how you

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:16.240
can't find a girlfriend 
that I can't work.

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:17.970
Stop making excuses!

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:20.070
But look over there.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:26.080
All of our visitors today are couples.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:27.220
It appears so.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:30.800
They're all sharing umbrellas lovingly.

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:35.850
The zoo on a rainy day is a great,
 little-known dating spot.

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:41.230
You sound like a dating expert,
but you don't even have a girlfriend.

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:44.020
Mind your own business!

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:49.050
You should stop reading tips on dating

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:50.450
and get to work.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.320
I don't read those!

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.320
And I'm not slacking off at work!

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:58.040
If you had a girlfriend, 
you'd be more enthusiastic at work.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:01.740
Well, to me, all of you at the zoo are

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:03.920
like my significant other.

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:09.040
Now you sound like a pure and
 innocent idol and I don't like it.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:14.350
Yeah. I don't want to hear 
idol-like phrases like

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:17.930
"I don't go to the bathroom."

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:24.110
True idols are like us and their 
poop smells like lemons.

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:27.900
Your conversation is drifting, Panda.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:33.060
Not to mention, no matter 
how much you like animals,

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:37.420
I think it'd be hard to be 
married to us animals.

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:39.340
W-What are you even talking about?

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:41.060
Listen, Mr. Handa.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:44.620
Mr. Full-time Panda, 
who's been divorced twice,

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:46.800
will now be your love advisor.

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.990
I leave it to you, advisor.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:54.340
I haven't been divorced twice.

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:59.470
Now I leave it to you, er... 
not advisor, but love hunter.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.800
That wasn't the part you 
were supposed to retract.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:06.010
Or rather, could you not push 
weird characterizations on me?

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:10.150
Anyways, I don't need 
any advice on love.

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:13.920
That's what he says, love leader.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:16.580
Don't call me "leader," either.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:21.510
But, Mr. Handa, would you be content 
with never having a girlfriend?

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:26.570
N-Never?

00:16:29.850 --> 00:16:31.600
Yeah...

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:38.560
Of course I want a girlfriend,

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:43.340
but at my age, I'd rather have a 
wife than a girlfriend.

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:46.110
It'll be okay.

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:48.270
You're a good person, Mr. Handa.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:50.560
P-Panda!

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:54.200
And you're the type that'll get 
nowhere as a good person.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:57.130
Yeah, someone no one cares about.

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:01.740
Oh, sorry.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:03.880
Cheer up.

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:08.750
There must be a girl out there who
will understand what a great person you are.

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:11.090
Y-You think so?

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:12.860
Of course.

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:15.300
There has to be at least one 
somewhere in the universe.

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:23.070
Just one... in the universe?

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:26.650
One is plenty.

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:32.370
If you can meet the one person 
you're destined to be with,

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:34.240
you don't need any more 
happiness than that.

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:36.510
Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:40.690
So, cheer up.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:42.540
We're on your side.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:45.560
Mr. Handa...

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:48.790
Is it okay to let pandas cheer you up?

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:54.590
Here, eat more, Panda.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:56.910
I'm good, thanks.

00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:58.660
Then, here, Polar Bear.

00:17:58.660 --> 00:17:59.510
I'm done, too.

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:02.580
Then...

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:04.220
We're fine.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:08.090
I gained weight again from eating
 too many of the

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:10.430
breads you buy, Mr. Penguin.

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:14.190
What are you talking about? Eat more.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.030
Because... See?

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:21.030
Miss Penko gave me free 
service tickets again.

00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:27.220
I'd be even happier if these 
tickets were for handshakes.

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.290
"Uhehe?"

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:35.380
If you laugh so pervertedly, 
Miss Penko won't like you.

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:37.640
How rude!

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:40.430
I didn't laugh like "uhehe."

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:44.120
Yeah, you totally didn't 
laugh like "uhehe."

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:45.800
Right?

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:47.240
It was "guhehe."

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:50.400
I didn't laugh like that.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:53.590
By the way,

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:55.590
the girls from our group 
blind date the other day

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:58.410
said they want to drink with 
you again, Mr. Handa.

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:00.110
Really?

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:04.120
Should I set something up again?

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:10.080
Well, eventually.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:14.850
Oh, all right.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:17.510
I'm going to head out.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.080
Okay. Thanks for all of your hard work.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:23.180
It's raining hard, so be careful.

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:24.660
I will.

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:27.470
You should head home soon, too.

00:19:28.170 --> 00:19:29.380
I will.

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:53.100
I forgot the cell phone 
you lent me, Mr. Handa.

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:56.100
I'm at Polar Bear's 
Café right now,

00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:58.380
so could you drop it off 
on your way home?

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:05.770
For crying out loud, Panda...

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:14.020
Hello.

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:17.720
That must have been rough.

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:19.710
I'll take your poncho for you.

00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:21.320
Oh, thank you.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:23.490
Here.

00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:26.470
Don't forget it from now on.

00:20:27.130 --> 00:20:29.010
Thank you.

00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:32.040
You're such a great guy, Mr. Handa.

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:33.950
Jeez.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:38.070
Could I relax here for a little bit?

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:39.170
Of course.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:45.000
And then, Miss Penko...

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:47.350
You just told us that.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:50.350
I wonder if love clouds the 
eyes of animals, too?

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:53.840
It wouldn't hurt for you to listen!

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:19.540
Are you awake?

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:25.700
I'm sorry! I must have dozed off.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:28.390
No need to worry.

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:30.640
This is on the house from the owner.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:54.330
It's so warm.

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:05.590
The green of the plants 
is so vivid after the rain.

00:22:06.080 --> 00:22:08.510
It's truly beautiful.

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:13.760
Yes.

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:25.370
Next Time

00:23:58.040 --> 00:23:59.750
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:01.020
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.020 --> 00:24:03.670
Tell me 500 cute things about me.

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:05.400
That's a difficult request.

00:24:05.400 --> 00:24:08.370
Then 499 will do.

00:24:08.370 --> 00:24:10.590
You don't understand 
how to compromise, do you?

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:11.450
Thanks!

00:24:11.450 --> 00:24:12.340
Sure.

00:24:12.340 --> 00:24:13.720
Then tell me...

00:24:13.720 --> 00:24:15.850
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:17.920
Next time Polar Bear's Café

00:24:17.920 --> 00:24:20.200
will be broadcasted on a 
station other than this one.

00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:22.550
You'll be able to watch 
it on this station!

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:24.480
Tanabata Decorations

00:24:22.550 --> 00:24:23.530
Enjoy!
